<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">A LITTLE HELP GOES A LONG WAY</div><h1>Your guide to a smoother day.</h1><p>The essentials for running your shop with confidence.</p></div></div><section class="panel form-panel"><div class="help-content"><section><h3>1. Make your workspace yours</h3><p>Administrators can change the business name, logo, contact details, timezone, currency, tax, and receipt footer in Business Settings. Choose your currency before your first order. Managers can set up the service catalog with prices per kilogram, piece, load, or pair.</p></section><section><h3>2. Receive a customer’s laundry</h3><ol><li>Add or find a customer in Customers. Keep their phone number and preferences up to date.</li><li>Select New order. Choose the customer and pickup date, then add services and quantities.</li><li>Record garment details, stains, care instructions, and a rack or bag label.</li><li>Check the total and create the order. Record a deposit or full payment on the details page.</li><li>Open Receipt / print to print a claim receipt or save it as a PDF using the browser print dialog.</li></ol></section><section><h3>3. Process the order</h3><p>Advance through Received → Washing → Drying → Folding → Ready for pickup. Each change records the staff member, time, and optional handover note. When the customer collects, collect the remaining balance and mark Completed. Processing cannot skip stages. Services that do not use every physical stage can advance through the unused stage with a note.</p></section><section><h3>4. Record a payment</h3><p>Verify that funds were received first. Enter the amount, method (cash, card, bank transfer, or e-wallet), and reference. Partial payments are supported; overpayments are rejected. Repeated submission of the same payment is protected against duplication. Card and e-wallet transactions take place outside this application.</p></section><section><h3>5. Handle cancellations and corrections</h3><p>Managers and administrators can cancel unpaid, unfinished orders with a reason. Order line items cannot change after creation, preserving price history. For a mistaken unpaid order, cancel it and create a corrected order. For a paid-order correction, use the refund workflow on its detail page, then cancel or replace the order as appropriate. Completed orders remain in the historical record.</p></section><section><h3>6. Keep supplies and expenses organized</h3><p>Use Inventory to add supplies and record stock received (+) or used (−), with a reason. Quantities never go below zero. Reorder warnings appear when on-hand stock reaches the reorder level. Consumption is manual. Use Expenses to record operating spending; Reports combines collections and expenses by date.</p></section><section><h3>7. Manage your team</h3><p>Administrators create accounts and choose roles in Team & Access. Share temporary passwords privately. New staff must change their password before accessing operations. Deactivate an account to remove access. Account changes revoke existing browser sessions. Staff can change their own password in My account.</p></section><section><h3>8. Read reports and protect your records</h3><p>Reports shows collections, expenses, net cash movement, booked order value, and all-time outstanding balances. Export payments to CSV for reconciliation. Net cash movement is not accounting profit. Back up the MySQL database, uploaded branding, and the application key regularly. Full setup, backup, recovery, and security instructions are in the project’s docs folder.</p></section></div></section>
